MAP_DELTA_PROPOSAL: {node: "CLAIM-0013", change: "status: HELD-conditional (L0 yellow, 5/5 yellow). Contribution narrowed to MEASUREMENT METHODOLOGY (anti-circular GT + matched-random control + conditional surface), NOT the gate concept itself. Gate-concept novelty unestablished vs SKR + semantic caching — requires citation/distinction + live prior-art sweep before L1. L1 requirements: real traces, real embedding, real LLM task accuracy, semantic-cache baseline. No promotion until prior-art gap closed."}
RATIONALE: Unanimous 5/5 YELLOW from a committee that engaged seriously with the evidence. The researcher's own "HELD-conditional" framing is honest and appropriate — this is the strongest aspect of the submission. Three findings drive the verdict:

(1) THE FRAMEWORK IS REAL BUT THE NUMBERS ARE NOT INDEPENDENTLY INFORMATIVE. Theory_skeptic's critique is the most penetrating and is unrebutted: redundancy fraction ~f(p_repeat, W) is algebra on the generative process, not a discovered constant; Jaccard AUC=1.0 at paraphrase=0 is tautological given keyword-core span construction; beating random-skip is the expected outcome of any above-chance classifier. The anti-circularity guard (item-id vs text separation via paraphrase_rate) is a genuine improvement over CLAIM-0008's circular failure, but it is PARTIAL — text is generated from item-id via shared keyword cores, and paraphrase_rate is the only thing breaking the deterministic link, so it parameterizes the confound rather than eliminating it. The scientific content is the framework + conditional map, not the headline numbers. The researcher mostly agrees with this framing.

(2) NOVELTY IS UNRESOLVED, NOT REFUTED. Novelty_killer was permission-blocked on live web search and explicitly cannot verify or rule out collisions against ≥2 independent sources. SKR ("do I already know this") and GPTCache (semantic query-cache hit detection via embedding overlap) are strong collision candidates on the core mechanism. The surviving novelty is the measurement methodology — matched-random-skip control + independent item-id redundancy GT — which is a modest but real contribution. The researcher's disclaimer of adaptive-retrieval novelty is honest and correct. But the gate-concept novelty (skip because answer is already in the live window) has NOT been distinguished from (a) SKR's "already-have-it" parametric-knowledge gate applied to in-context knowledge, or (b) semantic caching's structurally isomorphic overlap-based skip. These citations are MANDATORY before any future GREEN.

(3) THE MISSING BASELINE IS LOAD-BEARING. Evaluation_prosecutor's point that random-skip is a strawman when semantic query caching is the industry standard for cutting RAG redundancy costs is unrebutted. If a simple (query, result) cache captures the same redundant retrievals at equal or better Pareto efficiency, the specific "live window" contribution is falsified operationally. The L1 MUST include this head-to-head.

PROCEDURAL NOTE: Prior-art search is INADEQUATE (novelty_killer confirms tools were blocked). Per my mandate, I cannot emit GREEN without adequate prior-art search. Even setting this aside, the unanimous YELLOW from all five reviewers, with substantive unrebutted concerns (construct validity, missing semantic-cache baseline, unresolved novelty collisions), independently supports YELLOW. The researcher's intellectual honesty — pre-defended circularity, explicit limitations, appropriate "HELD-conditional" verdict, no overclaiming — is genuinely commendable and keeps this firmly out of RED. The L0 accomplished what an L0 should: it built a clean measurement framework, ran a characterization, and identified exactly what the L1 must close. YELLOW with a clear, achievable promotion path.
```
